 "title": "Cryptococcus neoformans and its interactions with CO2 and other organisms.",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around Cryptococcus neoformans, an organism that has various processes and interactions with other entities. It has Kex2p, a process or phenotype, and hemagglutinin (HA) glycoprotein, a chemical. CO2 has inhibitory effects on Candida tropicalis and germinates Scedosporium/Lomentospora. Cryptococcus neoformans interacts with influenza virus and is involved in Furin. The organism also expresses Kex2p and has capsule formation regulated by CO2. Other organisms, such as Candida albicans and Candida glabrata, undergo morphological changes in the presence of CO2. The cluster also includes various methods and tools, including MaxQuant, HADDOCK, and online capillary nanoLC-MS/MS.",
